edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186563173 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563620 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c42bbbe5-1f49-507b-a85b-15a0a5e80a99" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563632 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186562942 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563632 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186563034 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563632 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186563282 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563632 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186563352 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563632 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186563397 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563632 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563632 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563632 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186563352 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563632 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e4e9db8c-de87-5771-b057-8503dbc84d01" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563695 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186563557 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563695 #edb/ref 1069 "q-156691" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563695 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563695 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following diagrams shows the graph of $y={log}_{10}⁡x?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563695 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "66bc9e90-0e6b-5349-afc6-a4320dc355fe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563695 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's recall some of the basic properties of $y={log}_{10}⁡x:$\n\n- The domain is $x>0$, and the range is $-\\infty <y<\\infty .$\n\n- The graph has the vertical asymptote $x=0.$\n\n- The function is an increasing function.\n\n- The graph passes through the point $(1,0).$\n\n- For $x>1$, the graph is positive and grows very slowly as we increase $x.$ We say that $y\\to \\infty $ (slowly) as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nOf the given functions, the only one that has all of these properties is as follows:\n\n![](images/5a/5a52b4fcfb2cc410c894f69771ff450ceef1366048438345d1444e35186d9d76.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563710 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186563632 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563710 #edb/ref 1069 "q-69693" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563710 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563710 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following diagrams shows the graph of $y={log}_{2}⁡x?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563710 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "82de78d8-db02-58ba-afa8-a2bcae276094" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563710 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's recall some of the basic properties of $y={log}_{2}⁡x:$\n\n- The domain is $x>0$, and the range is $-\\infty <y<\\infty .$\n\n- The graph has the vertical asymptote $x=0.$\n\n- The function is an increasing function.\n\n- The graph passes through the point $(1,0).$\n\n- For $x>1$, the graph is positive and grows very slowly as we increase $x.$ We say that $y\\to \\infty $ (slowly) as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nOf the given functions, the only one that has all of these properties is as follows:\n\n![](images/28/285e69e8c0914643c1fb695d0146a5e83304d74f9e8fbd8efbc2100a7f32bd9e.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563715 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186563620 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563715 #edb/ref 1069 "q-156742" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563715 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563715 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y={log}_{8}⁡x?$\n\nI. The domain is $x\\ge 0$\n\nII. It has no horizontal asymptotes\n\nIII. It passes through the point $(64,2)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563715 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "96d6c320-22a1-578b-bc1b-575bf1a1c004" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563715 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's plot the graph of $y={log}_{8}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/68/6811e57f1259b97448811ac9abe8d6fc7f76a52b62e685f2fa0ec36e290381b4.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. From the graph, we see that the domain is $x>0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the function $y={log}_{8}⁡x$ has no horizontal asymptote. However, it does have the vertical asymptote $x=0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Substituting $x=64$ into the equation of the curve gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={log}_{8}⁡(64) \\\\  & ={log}_{8}⁡({8}^{2}) \\\\  & =2{log}_{8}⁡(8) \\\\  & =2\\,\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, only statements II and III are true." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563745 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186563539 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563745 #edb/ref 1069 "q-156696" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563745 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563745 #edb/ref 1071 "What's the range of $f(x)={log}_{10}⁡x?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563745 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d6e79644-f01f-5d41-959c-0424a55445f9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563745 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's recall the graph of $y={log}_{10}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/46/460a26a36316db034c93017f45aba301b1a39146b1dcb60b3024d3a20a824314.png)\n\nThe domain of $y={log}_{10}⁡x$ is $x\\in (0,\\infty )$ and the range is $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"All real numbers.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563747 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186563584 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563747 #edb/ref 1069 "q-156700" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563747 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563747 #edb/ref 1071 "What's the domain of $y={log}_{8}⁡x?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563747 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "db1e03ac-5baa-5855-b6ca-f2c610df9446" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563747 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's recall the graph of $y={log}_{8}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/8e/8e38a8edb560a0ddaa2e7802048ea0285e7bf3e72325de0a48f2672d9e81112c.png)\n\nThe domain of $y={log}_{8}⁡x$ is $x\\in (0,\\infty )$ and the range is $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x>0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
